{"name":"Gourmet Mushroom","hex":"#968d8c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gourmet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Fine; of superior quality. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A connoisseur in eating and drinking; someone who takes their food seriously."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gourmet"},{"term":"mushroom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the fleshy fruiting bodies of fungi typically produced above ground on soil or on their food sources (such as decaying wood).","A fungus producing such fruiting bodies."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having characteristics like those of a mushroom, for example in shape or appearance, speed of growth, or texture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mushroom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gourmet","blocks":[{"text":"Gourmet is a cultural idea associated with the culinary arts of fine food and drink, or haute cuisine, which is characterized by their high level of refined and elaborate food preparation techniques and displays of balanced meals that have an aesthetically pleasing presentation of several contrasting, often quite rich courses. Historically the ingredients used in the meal tended to be rare for the region, which could also be impacted by the local state and religious customs. The term and the related characteristics are typically used to describe people with more discerning palates and enthusiasm. Gourmet food is more frequently provided with small servings and in more upscale and posh fine dining establishments that cater to a more affluent and exclusive client base. When it comes to cooking gourmet dishes, there are also frequent cross-cultural interactions that introduce new, exotic, and expensive ingredients, materials, and traditions with more refined, complex, formal, and sophisticated high-level cooking and food preparation techniques."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gourmet","wikidata":"Q1458730"},{"title":"Mushroom","blocks":[{"text":"A mushroom is the fleshy, spore-bearing fruiting body of a fungus, typically produced above ground on soil or another food source. A toadstool generally refers to a poisonous mushroom."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Sparrige_Sch%C3%BCppling_%28Pholiota_squarrosa%29.jpg/330px-Sparrige_Sch%C3%BCppling_%28Pholiota_squarrosa%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mushroom","wikidata":"Q83093"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Zwerg_Postkarte_001.jpg/500px-Zwerg_Postkarte_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Zwerg_Postkarte_001.jpg/500px-Zwerg_Postkarte_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Amanita muscaria, the most easily recognised \"toadstool\", is frequently depicted in fairy stories and on greeting cards. It is often associated with gnomes.[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZwerg_Postkarte_001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Mushroom_cap_morphology2.png/500px-Mushroom_cap_morphology2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Mushroom_cap_morphology2.png/1280px-Mushroom_cap_morphology2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Mushroom_cap_morphology2.png/500px-Mushroom_cap_morphology2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Morphological characteristics of the caps of mushrooms","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMushroom_cap_morphology2.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.o